                     HOWARD ELIAS JOINS DIGITAL'S
                    PERSONAL COMPUTER BUSINESS UNIT
                    AS VICE PRESIDENT, DESKTOP LINE
         

MAYNARD, Mass. -- August 1, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation
today announced that Howard D. Elias has joined the company as vice
president, desktop product line, of Digital's Personal Computer
Business Unit, effective August 29, 1994. 
     
     Elias, 37, will manage all aspects of the PC Business Unit's 
desktop and deskside product families, including product management,
product development, engineering, and product marketing, worldwide. He
will report to Bernhard Auer, the vice president and general manager of
Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit, headquartered in Acton, 
Massachusetts.
    
     "As our desktop business continues to grow at a record-setting
pace, Digital is strengthening its management team with a leader from
the PC industry experienced in managing a high-volume product
environment," Auer stated. "Howard's credentials, broad experience,
and strong product management skills will contribute significantly to
meeting Digital's goal of becoming a top PC vendor by 1995," he added.
     
     "Digital's PC team is one of the most exciting places to be in the
PC industry today. I look forward to helping Digital extend its strong
brand equity into wider market segments, while leveraging the resources
of a refocused, more nimble, and more flexible company in the world of
client/server computing," Elias commented.
     
     Previously, Elias was vice president of worldwide marketing, and
general manager of the desktop line of business for AST Research, Inc.
of Irvine, California. Earlier, he spent over 16 years with Tandy
Corporation in a variety of management positions, including vice
president of sales and marketing; president (interim), GRID Systems;
vice president, corporate marketing; vice president, computer
merchandising, Radio Shack; director of OEM marketing, Tandy
Electronics; and various marketing and merchandising management
positions for Tandy International Electronics in Europe. A native of 
Detroit, Michigan, Elias attended Wayne State University in Detroit.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide
information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha AXP platforms, storage,
networking, software and services, together with industry-focused
solutions from business partners, help organizations compete and win in
today's global marketplace. 
				####
         
