           DIGITAL NAMES ANDRES CARVALLO GENERAL MANAGER
              FOR THE PERSONAL COMPUTER BUSINESS UNIT
                 IN LATIN AMERICA/CARIBBEAN REGION


ACTON, MA -- August 3, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced the appointment of Andres Carvallo as General Manager of 
the Personal Computer Business Unit for Latin America and the 
Caribbean, responsible for sales, operations and marketing.  He 
reports to Raymond Weadock, vice president and general manager for 
the Americas.  Carvallo will be based in Deerfield Beach, Florida.

     "Andres has a proven record of success in growing high-
technology businesses in Latin America.  His experience will be 
invaluable as Digital expands its operations to meet the rising 
demand for PCs in that region," said Weadock.

     Carvallo said "I come to Digital at an exciting time.  It is 
becoming established as a top PC manufacturer and the Digital name 
is recognized for its product quality and support.  I look forward 
to helping to accelerate Digital PC's success in Latin America and 
the Caribbean."

     Carvallo, a native of Venezuela, came to Digital from Borland 
International, Inc.  As General Manager for Latin America, he 
opened subsidiaries for Borland in Brazil, Chile and Argentina and 
started manufacturing operations in Mexico and Brazil.

     Prior to that, he was Regional Manager for Latin America for 
the Santa Cruz Operation, Inc., where he opened a subsidiary in 
Mexico and substantially increased the number of resellers of its 
UNIX operating system. Previously, Carvallo was U.S. Product 
Marketing Manager for DOC and Windows products at Microsoft Corporation.

     The Digital Personal Computer Business Unit features a wide 
range of systems from notebooks to desktops and servers based on 
Intel i486 and Pentium-based processors.  In the past year, sales 
and unit shipments have doubled with revenue exceeding $1 billion.  
PCs are sold through a direct sales force, catalog, resellers and 
distributors.  A three-year warranty and support program is 
standard.

     Carvallo received bachelor of science degrees in Business and 
Mechanical Engineering from the University of Kansas and completed 
Stanford University's management program.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Alpha AXP platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
