                     WIM ELFRINK JOINS DIGITAL
           AS VICE PRESIDENT AND GENERAL MANAGER FOR THE
             PERSONAL COMPUTER BUSINESS UNIT IN EUROPE


MAYNARD, Mass. -- August 15, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that Wim Elfrink has joined the company as vice 
president and general manager of the Personal Computer Business 
Unit's European operations, based in Geneva.

     Elfrink, 42, will be responsible for all operational aspects 
of the Personal Computer Business Unit in Europe, effective 
September 1, 1994.  He succeeds, and will report to, Bernhard Auer 
who was recently promoted to lead Digital's worldwide Personal 
Computer Business Unit. 

     In his hew responsibilities Elfrink will manage Digital's 
personal computer business in Western Europe, Eastern Europe, North 
Africa and the Middle East.  He will be responsible for business 
strategy, sales, marketing, distribution and business development.  
Elfrink will also serve as a member of Digital's European 
Management Team which coordinates the company's overall European 
business activities.

     "Digital is quickly becoming one of the leading personal 
computer vendors in Europe," commented Bernhard Auer, vice 
president and general manager for Digital's Personal Computer 
Business Unit.  "We sought a leader who will continue the momentum 
and bring Digital into the forefront of the industry in Europe -- 
we have found that leader in Wim Elfrink." 

     Elfrink brings to Digital a well-rounded portfolio which 
includes management experience in engineering, marketing, customer 
and sales support, as well as strong general management skills.  
Most recently, he was European Marketing Director, Personal 
Information Products for Hewlett Packard, headquartered in 
Grenoble.  Previously, as the HP Country Manager for the Computer 
Products Organization, he established the European Customer Support 
Center in the Netherlands.   

     Prior to joining HP as the Netherlands Country Support Manager 
in 1986, he held positions in technical product management, sales 
support and distribution, and field management at both Rank Xerox 
and Olivetti, including international assignments with worldwide 
responsibility in both the US and Italy for Rank Xerox and 
Olivetti, respectively.

