                 DIGITAL BRINGS NEW ENHANCEMENTS TO
                         MARKET ON OpenVMS


        OpenVMS achieves highest open standard certification
        with XPG4 branding -- beating all major competitors


        New OpenVMS Management Station V1.0, allows OpenVMS
             management from a single Windows-based PC

            
MAYNARD, Mass. -- August 19, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
recently announced the OpenVMS operating system is ahead of its 
competitors in attaining XPG4 branding and introduced a significant 
enhancement to the operating system.

     Digital introductions included the fact that the OpenVMS 
operating systems for both VAX and Alpha AXP computers have been 
awarded XPG4 Base Branding certification by X/Open Ltd., the 
non-profit open standards consortium that certifies software 
systems for compliance to rigorous standardization requirements. 
Additionally, a new OpenVMS management tool, the OpenVMS
Management Station V1.0, was introduced. 

OpenVMS AXP and OpenVMS VAX OPERATING SYSTEMS ACHIEVE XPG4 BASE BRANDING

     Digital's OpenVMS operating system significantly increased its 
open systems standards compliance, with the XPG4 Base Branding 
Award of Certification.  XPG4 is the current release of the X/Open 
Portability Guide, that asserts 11,528 rigorous tests, as part of 
the verification/branding process. 

     "We are extremely proud of this achievement by our OpenVMS 
operating system," said Jesse Lipcon, vice president of OpenVMS 
systems and servers. "Customers who are implementing open systems 
will typically look for the XPG4 brand as a proof point that a 
vendor's software is verified as being open, by an unbiased
certifier, X/Open. We also find that many users actually specify 
XPG-conformance in their procurement. 

     "The OpenVMS operating system achieved XPG3 Base Branding two 
years ago, before any other major non UNIX system in the world," 
continued Lipcon.  "Today, major vendors have announced their 
intention to seek XPG3 branding - including IBM for the AS400 and 
ES9000 MVS as well as HP for MPE - but they have not achieved the 
XPG3 branding. The OpenVMS operating system leaps ahead with XPG4. 
Furthermore, the OpenVMS operating system has achieved this
significant open systems milestone ahead of many popular 
competitive UNIX offerings, including IBM's AIX and Sun's Solaris 
operating systems." 

OpenVMS MANAGEMENT STATION V1.0

     In keeping with Digital's goal to bring PC ease-of-use to 
OpenVMS system management tasks, Digital is now shipping the 
Management Station V1.0 for the OpenVMS operating system. According 
to Lipcon, "This is a tool that allows customers to manage one or 
more cluster systems from a single Windows-based PC,thus bringing 
cluster management into the common Microsoft Windows GUI (graphical 
user interface) environment." 
AVAILABILITY

     OpenVMS Management Station V1.0 is available now, and will be 
bundled with the next OpenVMS operating system release for VAX and 
Alpha AXP in late 1994.

PRICING

     There is no charge for the OpenVMS Management Station V1.0 the 
license. The one-time charge for the user media documentation set 
is $99.00.  It will be bundled with the OpenVMS operating system 
license, with the next version of the OpenVMS operating system.

     X/Open is an independent, worldwide, open systems organization 
supported by the world's largest information systems suppliers,
user organizations, and software companies. Its mission is to bring
to users greater value from computing, through the practical
implementation of open systems.

