introduced four new text terminals, including its first fully-
functional color text terminals.  The introduction of the VT520 
Multi-Session Monochrome and VT525 Color Multi-Session terminals 
rounds out the VT500 product family.  The Dorio 20 Multi-Session 
Monochrome and the Dorio 25 Color Multi-Session terminals complete 
the Dorio family.

     All four terminals add leading edge functionality that is new 
to the market:  the ability to run truly independent multiple 
sessions simultaneously. Formerly, no companies terminals were able 
to run more than two sessions at one time.  Now, with the 
introduction of the VT520 and the Dorio 20 terminals, four sessions 
can run in monochrome at one time; while the VT525 and the Dorio 25 
terminals enable four sessions to run in color.  The sessions can 
be viewed on a split screen with two sessions visible, enabling 
visual integration of information and improved productivity.  

     Both the VT525 and the Dorio 25 terminals bring instant color 
to existing monochrome applications.  The color is especially 
advantageous for forms applications, process and alarm situations, 
as well as in distinguishing one session from another.

     "With the addition of the VT520, VT525, Dorio 20 and Dorio 25 
terminals, our terminal families provide an open solution for any 
text terminal need, whether ANSI, ASCII, or PCTerm," said Larry 
Cabrinety, vice president of the Components & Peripherals Business 
Unit.  "And, all of our terminals are built with traditional 
Digital quality, backed by our world class service and support." 

     The new VT520 and Dorio 20 monochrome model electronics are 
housed within the monitor.  VT525 and Dorio 25 color model 
electronics are housed in a separate systems box and offer a choice 
of PC style color monitor sizes -- 14", 15" or 17".  All monochrome 
models feature an industry leading 3-year warranty. The color 
models include a 3-year warranty for the systems box and keyboard, 
and a 1-year warranty for the PC style color monitors.  In 
addition, all the VT500 and Dorio models are ISO 9002 certified, 
guaranteeing an international measure of manufacturing quality.

     "There is a vast number of industries as well as government 
agencies that use text terminals for their daily activities.  Our 
new terminals provide users with features that will last, including 
improved ergonomics and Energy Star, which provides advanced 
energy-saving functionality," said Brian Fitzgerald, vice president 
of the C&P's video business.  "In addition, these terminals provide 
leading technologies such as, framed sessions, dynamic page 
allocation, and session status indicators, at an affordable price.  
And, all terminals deliver ease of use along with quality 
workmanship to users, regardless of what industry they are in."

     Both families of terminals have common functionality, 
supporting more than 30 operating systems and 16-18 terminal 
emulations.  Seventy-three ergonomically designed keyboards support 
25 different languages, for use in North and South America, Eastern 
and Western Europe, and much of the Pacific Rim.  All keyboards are 
fully remappable and programmable to eight levels.  The new 
products all feature windows-like setup in 5-languages, along with 
a clock, calculator and programmable banner.  In addition, the 
terminals, including their packaging, are fully recyclable.

     The VT525 and Dorio 25 terminals provide full color text 
capability featuring 16 colors out of a palette of 4096 per 
session.  Both color terminals are available with a range of color 
monitors of 14, 15 or 17 inches.

     The new Dorio 20 and 25 terminals, like the Dorio 10 terminal, 
provide the same features as the VT500 series, and include a serial 
port 9-pin connector appropriate for use in UNIX, SCO UNIX, and 
ASCII/PCTerm environments.

     The new multi-session monochrome terminals, the VT520 and 
Dorio 20 terminals, are currently available and have a suggested 
list price starting at $499.  The color multi-session VT525 and 
Dorio 25 terminals are also currently available and have a 
suggested list price starting at $649.  Additional information can 
be obtained by calling 1-800-777-4343.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
