                     RED BRICK WAREHOUSE SHIPS
                   FOR DIGITAL ALPHA AXP SYSTEMS


     ... Leading data warehouse solution for open client/server
            environments strengthens Digital's mainframe
                    downsizing capabilities ...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- August 25, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
and Red Brick Systems, of Los Gatos, California, today announced 
the immediate availability of Red Brick Warehouse on Digital's 
Alpha AXP systems running the DEC OSF/1 UNIX based operating 
system. Pricing begins at US$20,000. 

     Customers such as those migrating from legacy mainframe 
environments will find that Red Brick Warehouse offers the 
economics of implementing large-scale data warehouse solutions 
with the superior performance of Alpha AXP systems. 

     "Red Brick Warehouse is the first industry-standard relational 
database management system (RDBMS) architected specifically for 
open client/server data warehouse environments," said Michael 
Carabetta, Digital vice president of Cross Industries Marketing. 
"Add the unsurpassed price-performance of Alpha AXP and OSF/1, and 
we have a winning solution for the growing data warehouse market," 
he added. 

     According to AJ Brown, vice president of marketing at Red 
Brick Systems, "IS and business managers can improve the quality 
and performance of their business management applications across 
the entire line of Alpha AXP systems running Red Brick Warehouse. 
For example, the new DEC 2100 Server running Red Brick Warehouse 
provides an ideal low-cost Alpha AXP entry point, scalable to the 
largest Alpha AXP data warehousing solution."

Emerging Need for Data Warehousing

     The data warehousing concept arose from the growing 
competitive need to quickly analyze huge amounts of business 
information. Data warehousing overcomes the limitations of 
conventional database systems by providing:

     o	A consistent interface into the diverse systems on which 
        the data resides.
             
     o	Lower costs and increased flexibility associated with 
        client/server environments.
             
     o	Robust query performance.
     
     o	Historical data on-line.

     As a result, corporate information is more accessible to 
management. A data warehouse stores all the current and historical 
data from disparate operational systems that business decision 
makers need. This makes data readily accessible to the people who 
need it without tying up front-line operational resources.

     These developments are defining a new database market called 
data warehousing. The size and growth of data warehousing in the 
'90s will rival that of OLTP in the '80s. 

     For the growing number of customers across many industries, 
such as those moving applications off mainframes, data warehousing 
offers a particularly attractive improvement over conventional 
database solutions.

Red Brick Warehouse

     Red Brick Warehouse is the first and only RDBMS optimized for 
data warehousing. Unlike RDBMS products optimized for on-line 
transaction processing, Red Brick Warehouse enables:

     o	Fast development and deployment of business management 
        applications.
             
     o	Querying of very large databases of information gathered 
        from disparate sources. 
             
     o	Superior access to consolidated and detailed business 
        information.
             
     o	Fast performance.
             
     Operating in an open client/server environment, Red Brick 
Warehouse is a breakthrough in speed and flexibility for data 
analysis. Red Brick Warehouse is the only RDBMS to:
             
     o	Process business queries 10 times faster than traditional 
        RDBMSs.
             
     o	Perform complex business analysis without extensive 
        application development.
             
     o	Support the use of informational data  for business 
        analysis with low administrative costs.
             
     Users can access data stored in Red Brick Warehouse through 
industry-standard SQL, which provides compatibility with existing 
applications. Or they can use Red Brick's extension to SQL, RISQL. 
RISQL augments SQL with a variety of powerful operations 
appropriate to data analysis and decision support applications, 
e.g., ranking, moving averages, comparisons, market share, this 
year vs. last year.

Alpha AXP and DEC OSF/1 Systems

     Digital's Alpha AXP family of RISC-based, binary-compatible 
workstations and servers employs the world's most powerful micro-
processor architecture to deliver superior performance and 
scalability.  Alpha AXP systems are available in one- to six-
processor configurations and offer processing power unmatched in 
each price class. 

     The Alpha AXP platform is an ideal environment for customers 
downsizing from traditional mainframe systems to gain the 
flexibility, cost-effectiveness and performance of open client/
server solutions. 

     The DEC OSF/1 platform provides the industry's most robust, 
complete, standards-compliant commercial operating environment.  
DEC OSF/1 software supports symmetric multiprocessing, a wide range 
of cluster functionality, and total compatibility across Digital's 
family of Alpha AXP workstations and servers, from desktop systems 
to large multiprocessing systems. 

     Red Brick Systems is the leading provider of relational 
database products and services for data warehouse applications. The 
company specializes in software products used for business 
management applications and for ad hoc decision support where large 
client/server databases are the norm, usually tens of gigabytes in 
size with hundreds of millions of records. These applications 
require historical context and accurate, timely analysis of complex 
data relationships for both consolidated and detailed business 
information.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace. 
Digital is a leader in enabling organizations to downsize from 
mainframe platforms for improved flexibility and price-performance.
