   DIGITAL TO PROVIDE WORLDWIDE USERS OF MICROSOFT PRODUCTS WITH
              COMPREHENSIVE LOCAL SUPPORT AND SERVICES


MAYNARD, Mass. -- August 25, 1994 -- Users of popular Microsoft 
business products now have direct access to comprehensive, 
localized and timely service and support from Digital Equipment 
Corporation's Multivendor Customer Service organization, under 
terms of an agreement announced today between Digital and Microsoft 
Corporation.

     The agreement, naming Digital as a worldwide Authorized 
Support Center (ASC), is a unique certification within the 
Microsoft Solution Provider Program.  All ASC providers must meet 
stringent Microsoft standards for service competency, quality and 
customer satisfaction.

     Among the Microsoft products supported as part of the 
agreement are its personal operating systems, advanced systems and 
application software.

     "We are pleased to partner with Digital as a worldwide 
authorized support center," said Deborah Willingham, vice president 
of support at Microsoft. "Digital's multivendor support offerings and 
on-site services, coupled with their worldwide reach, will provide 
corporate customers using Microsoft products support they need to 
successfully implement mission-critical appliations in an open 
system environment."

     "Our selection as an ASC extends the decade-long partnership 
we've had with Microsoft," said John Rando, vice president of 
Digital's Multivendor Customer Services organization. "Over the 
last ten years, we've successfully serviced and supported 
Microsoft's customers through a number of relationships and 
programs. This latest agreement, which increases the access Digital 
has to internal Microsoft resources, reflects Microsoft's 
confidence that we can continue to support their customers' 
multivendor environments."  

     The agreement gives Digital's 29 support centers in 100 
countries the clearance to deal directly with Microsoft's worldwide 
subsidiaries.  Such close access to local Mircosoft expertise 
enhances Digital's ability to provide better, more timely localized 
service to Mircosoft customers. 

     The portfolio of services Digital will provide and deliver to 
Microsoft customers will focus on mission-critical support services 
for corporate customers.  In addition, Digital will provide 
installation and startup services, user support services, help desk 
support services and training on Microsoft products. 

     Sold through its direct and indirect sales channels, Digital's 
ASC capability entitles customers to receive, for one low price, 
service on all products, applications and technology Digital 
supports. This gives customers an affordable and carefully managed 
way to maintain their entire IT environments.

     Founded in 1975, Microsoft (NASDAQ "MSFT") is the worldwide 
leader in software for personal computers.  The company offers a 
wide range of products and services for business and personal use, 
each designed with the mission of making it easier and more 
enjoyable for people to take advantage of the full power of 
personal computing every day.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
