             High-Speed LAN Access Eases Network Jams...


            DIGITAL ANNOUNCES HIGH-PERFORMANCE, 100MBPS
                 PCI FAST ETHERNET CONTROLLER CHIP


   ...Also Enhances 10Mbps PCI Ethernet Chip With New Features...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- August 29, 1994 -- Digital Semiconductor, a 
Digital Equipment Corporation business, today announced the world's 
first PCI Fast Ethernet LAN controller chip, designed to link 
computers based on the Peripheral Components Interconnect (PCI) bus 
to high-speed local area networks.  The DECchip 21140 PCI Fast 
Ethernet LAN controller is a high-performance, highly integrated 
device with both 100Mbps and 10Mbps (megabit-per-second) ports, 
offering manufacturers of Ethernet interface cards, PCs, and 
servers the most compatible and cost-effective path to upgrade 
current products for Fast Ethernet connectivity.

     Digital also announced the DECchip 21040A, a new version of 
its 21040 PCI Ethernet LAN controller.  The DECchip 21040A 
controller features the industry's first implementation of NWay 
full-duplex autodetection, flash memory support, and support for 
universal voltage PCI systems.  It retains complete driver-
compatibility with the current DECchip 21040 device.

Fast Ethernet Combats Network Overload

     "Today's local area networks are under increasing pressure 
from the proliferation of network devices and the demands on 
network bandwidth posed by imaging, graphics and multimedia 
applications," said Philip Lozowick, Digital's PCI Ethernet product 
marketing manager.  "Fast Ethernet technology furnishes the 
bandwidth necessary to eliminate many of the overloads and delays 
caused by heavy message traffic.  It is also the most direct, least 
costly upgrade solution for Ethernet users.

     "Digital's DECchip 21140 PCI Fast Ethernet controller provides 
the easiest and fastest route from 10BaseT to 100BaseT Ethernet in 
PCI-based, mixed-platform, mixed-operating system environments," 
Lozowick added.  "The combination of PCI and Fast Ethernet puts 
server-level network performance right on the desktop."

     Digital was one of the original developers of Ethernet and 
participated in development of Fast Ethernet, in addition to being 
one of the early supporters of the PCI bus.  According to Art 
Swift, vice president, Semiconductor Marketing and Sales, "Digital 
has supplied the merchant chip market with innovative, 
high-performance PCI products.  The DECchip 21040, for example, is 
today's PCI Ethernet market leader.

     "All our PCI chips support all of the industry's major RISC 
and CISC microprocessor designs," Swift noted.

High Performance, Wide Compatibility

     The DECchip 21140 PCI Fast Ethernet LAN controller compatibly 
extends Digital's family of PCI Ethernet controllers with higher 
performance. The DECchip 21140 uses the same comprehensive set of 
software drivers as the DECchip 21040 and 21040A controllers, 
supporting Novell's NetWare, Microsoft's LANmanager, Windows NT, 
SCO UNIX, PATHWORKS, OSF/1, OpenVMS and other environments.  This 
enables adapter card manufacturers to build a single product that 
will work without modification with a wide range of hardware and 
software platforms.

     The DECchip 21140 PCI Fast Ethernet controller is priced at 
$39.50 in quantities of 5,000.  Samples will be available in 
October, with volume production ramp by the end of the year.

Integration Simplifies Product Design

     The new controller's high level of integration makes adapter 
design straightforward and less expensive.  The Physical Coding 
Sublayer (PCS) and scrambler are present on the chip to reduce the 
cost of 100BaseTX solutions.  Large, on-chip FIFO memory buffers 
eliminate the need for external buffers.  The 100Mbps port contains 
a complete MII interface to support voice-grade (CAT3) and data 
grade (CAT5) unshielded twisted pair, shielded twisted pair (STP), 
and fiber cabling.

     Like the DECchip 21040, the DECchip 21140 controller features 
a direct memory access (DMA) architecture optimized for efficient 
CPU utilization, and is also well suited to internetworking 
applications such as Ethernet switching, bridges, and routers that 
require connection to Fast Ethernet.  It supports full-duplex 
operation for high performance on Fast Ethernet fiber links of up 
to two kilometers between switches or routers.

     Evaluation kits will be available in October to help hardware 
engineers design products based on the DECchip 21140 controller and 
bring them to market more quickly.  Each kit contains a PCI 
Ethernet board, sample drivers, schematics, and a complete 
documentation set.

Flash Memory Support for DECchip 21040A

     In addition to NWay autodetection, Digital's new DECchip 
21040A PCI Ethernet chip supports flash memory to enable loading of 
remote boot ROM code and the opportunity to include vendor-
specific, added-value differentiation.  A 3.3V chip with 
5.0V-compatible I/O, the DECchip 21040A can be used to build 
universal add-in cards that work in both PCI system voltage 
signaling environments.  It also supports an energy-conserving 
power-down mode. 

     Priced at $24.50 in quantities of 5,000, the DECchip 21040A 
PCI Ethernet controller will be available for sampling in November 
and in volume during the first quarter of 1995.

     Digital Semiconductor, a Digital Equipment Corporation 
business headquartered in Hudson, Massachusetts, designs, 
manufactures and markets industry-leading semiconductor products, 
including Alpha AXP microprocessors and PCI-based peripheral chips, 
at fabrication facilities in Hudson, Massachusetts, and South 
Queensferry, Scotland.  Digital's Semiconductor Business also 
operates design centers in Hudson; Palo Alto, California; Austin, 
Texas; and Jerusalem, Israel.  A new, $450-million semiconductor 
fabrication facility with sub-half-micron capability is nearing 
completion in Hudson.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
