           DIGITAL EXTENDS BREADTH OF STACKABLE OFFERINGS
                BY BRINGING ENTERPRISE FUNCTIONALITY
            TO LOW-END ENVIRONMENTS AT AFFORDABLE PRICE


     New Ethernet Repeater and Reduced-Price Management Module
              Provide Intelligent, Flexible Solutions

 
MAYNARD, MA -- August 29, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation's 
Network Product Business today took steps to bring new enterprise 
functionality to its low-end networking offerings.  Digital 
announced an addition to its intelligent DEChub family, the 
DECrepeater 90TS, for small workgroups and departments within large
enterprises.  In addition, Digital announced more affordable hub 
management by reducing the price of network management hardware by 
34%, from $2255 to $1495.  

     Digital's DEChub products are aimed at the growing market for 
low-cost, "intelligent stackable" network solutions that provide a 
level of functionality formerly associated only with high-end hubs.  
Until recently, the network market was divided into low-
functionality stackables, for smaller workgroups, driven by price 
per port, and high-end, high-capacity hubs, driven by functionality 
and performance.  

     "While other network vendors are racing to put high-end 
intelligence into their stackable products, Digital, with its 
single integrated DEChub family, has offered intelligent stackable 
network solutions for some time," said William L. Maro, vice 
president, Network Product Marketing and Engineering.  Maro added,
"Unlike customers who have other vendors' products, Digital 
customers are not bound solely to stackables or to hub solutions 
they quickly outgrow.  Our uniquely flexible DEChub family allows 
modules to operate as stand-alone devices, be stacked with other 
modules, or be integrated into low- or high-density hubs, 
protecting the customer's investment."

High Functionality Ethernet Repeater

     A true eight-port 10BaseT repeater, the DECrepeater 90TS 
combines full SNMP management and Ethernet per-port security for 
building PC LANs or interconnecting to larger Ethernet LANs.  At 
$1155, the module provides high functionality and repeater 
management at an affordable price.  

     With built-in SNMP management, the DECrepeater 90TS provides 
detailed statistical monitoring and control at the port level.  The 
module can be managed by HUBwatch, a point and click hub management 
application, from either a PC or a workstation.  The DECrepeater 
90TS's port-level security provides protection against both 
broadcast intrusion and eavesdropping, thus preventing the 
transmission of data to and from unauthorized devices.  In the 
future, Digital will provide additional functionality to the 
DECrepeater 90TS through firmware upgrades.

     The DECrepeater 90TS is part of Digital's family of Ethernet 
repeaters, which offer between eight and 32 ports; a variety of 
standards-based media, including 10BaseT, 10BaseFL fiber, shielded 
twisted pair, ThinWire, and ThickWire.  

     Like all DEChub modules, the DECrepeater 90TS can be 
configured as a stand-alone solution, can be 'racked and stacked' 
as new users are added to the network and can snap into both the 
DEChub 90 and the DEChub 900 MultiSwitch.  This unique capability 
allows users to extend the network and increase functionality while
preserving their original investment.

     One of the early users of the DECrepeater 90TS is TAFE New 
South Wales (NSW), provider of vocational education and training in 
Australia with more than 400,000 students enrolling each year.  It 
has 152 sites connected to its network, which vary in size from 
campuses with 100 students to centers with 1500 staff and 35,000 
students.  Many TAFE campuses are in remote locations, furtherest
some 1000 kilometres from the support center.

     "TAFE NSW needed a solution that could be deployed into any of 
our sites regardless of their size", said Michael Anderton, TAFE's 
communications manager.  "The DECrepeater 90TS units were chosen 
because they were scalable, flexible, secure and easily managed."  
TAFE NSW is in the process of installing 400 DECrepeater 90TS's 
across the network.

Affordable Management for DEChub 90 Modules

     Digital has also reduced the price of its DECagent 90 SNMP 
management module by 34%, from $2255 to $1495.  The price reduction 
of the DECagent allows users to easily upgrade from simple 
connectivity to a fully managed solution. 

     The features of the DECagent 90 include graphical MIB 
II-compliant SNMP in-band and out-of-band management; the ability 
to support multiple communities and stand-alone modules; 
enterprise traps including security, error, population, and status 
change; and nonvolatile error logging of errors, upgrades, and 
factory resets.

     The DECagent 90 is used in conjunction with the HUBwatch 
management application.  "This new price makes it even easier and 
more affordable for customers to manage multiple DEChub devices," 
said Maro.  A single DECagent 90 can manage multiple repeaters, 
access servers, bridges and routers in a variety of stand-alone and
DEChub 90-based configurations across an extended LAN, resulting in 
significant management cost savings.  

     When combined with the limited time $1995 DEChub starter pack 
offer (an eight-slot DEChub 90 and three DECrepeater 90T UTP 
modules) which is being extended through December 30, 1994, Digital 
provides users with an exceptionally low-price point for full 
function manageable connectivity.  The extra five slots in the 
DEChub 90 allow plenty of room to expand by adding more modules.  
As users' networking needs grow, the modules can be removed from 
the DEChub 90 and snapped into the high-end DEChub 900 MultiSwitch. 

     The DECrepeater 90TS, the DECagent 90, and the network starter 
package are all available now.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
